editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. v. 3."},{"id":"0e331b73b8d4","b":"ECC","v":"npnf.athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","w":"athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":3,"p":[36,36],"r":[6,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hosius is called by Athan, the father and the president of the Council. Hist. Arian. 15. 16. Roman controversialists here explain why Hosius does not sign himself as the Pope's legate. De Marc. Concord. v. 4. Alber. Dissert. ix. and Protestants why his legates rank before all the other Bishops, even before Protogenes. Bishop of the place. Basnage, Ann. 347. 5. Febronius considers that Hosius signed here and at Nicaea, as a sort of representative of the civil, and the Legates of ecclesiastical supremacy. de Stat. Eccl. vi. 4. And so Thomassin, \"Imperator velut exterior Episcopus: praefuit autem summus Pontifex, ut Episcopus interior.\" Dissert. in Conc. x. 14. The popes never attended in person the Eastern Councils. St. Leo excuses himself on the plea of its being against usage. Epp. 37. and 93. [Silvester's absence from Nic`a was due solely to extreme old age. But Sardica was a Western council.]"},{"id":"5fd8b10e738b","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","w":"athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":4,"p":[9,9],"r":[2,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. ii. 9."},{"id":"0033ff73ca73","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","w":"athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":4,"p":[21,21],"r":[9,36],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Matt. ix. 36."},{"id":"d99240c22445","b":"SIR","v":"npnf.athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","w":"athanasius.apologia_contra_arianos","a":"athanasius_von_alexandrien","s":5,"p":[18,18],"r":[30,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"low","cited":"Ecclus. 30. 4.","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englis